WEBVTT

00:00:11.130 --> 00:00:12.880
Dynamic jumps.

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:17.010
Powerful moves.

00:00:19.630 --> 00:00:21.760
Smiles suspended in space.

00:00:27.670 --> 00:00:33.590
They support everyone,
inspire them, make them smile.

00:00:43.510 --> 00:00:47.760
It was like the sun lighting up the whole world.

00:01:03.340 --> 00:01:06.010
Sis, go for it!

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:12.550
Gooo!

00:01:12.550 --> 00:01:14.920
Haru, sit down.

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:18.590
Haru?

00:01:18.590 --> 00:01:20.510
I-I'm fine.

00:01:20.510 --> 00:01:25.510
Man, you only ever raise your voice
when you're cheering for Haruko.

00:01:28.130 --> 00:01:31.090
Sis, now! Nooow!

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:35.670
One point!

00:01:35.670 --> 00:01:37.760
She did it! She won!

00:01:37.760 --> 00:01:41.760
Your sister's freaking amazing!

00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:43.380
Sorry.

00:01:43.380 --> 00:01:46.300
Really, Kazu, I feel fine.

00:01:48.510 --> 00:01:50.260
<b>Bandou</b>
Meishiin
University

00:01:50.260 --> 00:01:51.460
That's my girl!

00:01:50.260 --> 00:01:52.760
Haruko Bandou Judo

00:01:50.260 --> 00:01:52.760
Haru

00:01:50.260 --> 00:01:52.760
Ku

00:01:51.460 --> 00:01:52.760
Haruko!

00:01:53.840 --> 00:01:56.880
My parents are so embarrassing.

00:01:56.880 --> 00:02:03.380
Well, c'mon, this is Meishiin University's
first win ever for its Women's Judo Club!

00:02:03.380 --> 00:02:07.090
And of course Haruko would be the one to do it.

00:02:12.460 --> 00:02:13.840
Incidentally,

00:02:13.840 --> 00:02:17.880
this is the first time I've ever watched
a match without my uniform on.

00:02:20.170 --> 00:02:22.130
You're almost there, Captain!

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:22.280
Caf Sunflower

00:02:22.130 --> 00:02:24.380
C'mon, eat up, eat up!

00:02:24.380 --> 00:02:26.880
--Faster, hurry!
--In 20 minutes there'd better not be a single crumb left!

00:02:26.910 --> 00:02:29.340
Captain, don't give up!

00:02:26.910 --> 00:02:29.170
<b>Finish your meal
in 20 minutes
and it's on the house</b>

00:02:29.340 --> 00:02:30.840
Captain!

00:02:31.840 --> 00:02:34.260
Go! You can do it!

00:02:34.260 --> 00:02:35.800
Captain, fight!

00:02:35.800 --> 00:02:38.960
Judo Club

00:02:35.800 --> 00:02:36.380
Captain, fight!

00:02:36.380 --> 00:02:38.960
Curry's practically a liquid!

00:02:40.630 --> 00:02:43.050
Hey, it's Bandou's little brother.

00:02:43.050 --> 00:02:45.210
--You came? Good job.
--Water!

00:02:49.510 --> 00:02:53.630
Geez, answer them with some energy, Haruki.

00:02:53.630 --> 00:02:56.920
How can you be so shy
now that you're in college?

00:02:58.130 --> 00:02:59.670
Mom and Dad?

00:02:59.670 --> 00:03:01.010
Went home already.

00:03:01.010 --> 00:03:04.300
Said they wanted to seriously
rethink tomorrow's training schedule.

00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:05.670
Where's Kazu?

00:03:05.670 --> 00:03:07.880
Off to visit his grandma.

00:03:07.880 --> 00:03:09.170
Okay.

00:03:11.960 --> 00:03:13.590
Sis.

00:03:13.590 --> 00:03:17.460
Congrats. You looked so cool out there.

00:03:17.460 --> 00:03:21.130
What? Quit it! That came out of nowhere!

00:03:21.130 --> 00:03:23.760
It's because you were cheering me on.

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:26.670
I could hear your voice.

00:03:26.670 --> 00:03:29.090
Always, always...

00:03:29.090 --> 00:03:32.590
Your cheering has a kind of power behind it.

00:03:34.670 --> 00:03:36.050
Haruki.

00:03:38.420 --> 00:03:39.920
Everything'll work out.

00:03:39.920 --> 00:03:41.880
Your shoulder will heal right up.

00:03:45.090 --> 00:03:47.760
Welp, time's up!

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:49.300
Damn it!

00:03:49.300 --> 00:03:55.840
--Somebody, lend me some cash! I need more money!
--Captain, please finish up before I retire!

00:03:55.840 --> 00:03:58.300
--Pay up already!
--Captain!

00:03:58.300 --> 00:04:00.300
Kohinata Hospital

00:04:01.550 --> 00:04:02.760
Here.

00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:05.420
Granny, I peeled an apple for you.

00:04:05.420 --> 00:04:06.920
Ah, that looks tasty.

00:04:06.920 --> 00:04:08.550
What a good grandson.

00:04:08.550 --> 00:04:10.840
Oh, would you like one?

00:04:10.840 --> 00:04:14.420
--I'm fine, thank you.
--Now the Lucky Seven are finally

00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:18.090
about to enter the 7th inning...

00:04:18.090 --> 00:04:19.800
Kasu...

00:04:33.880 --> 00:04:36.330
ＢＡＮＤＯＵ ＤＯＪＯ

00:04:33.880 --> 00:04:36.380
Judo Club

00:04:35.370 --> 00:04:37.380
Bandou Gym

00:04:37.550 --> 00:04:39.670
Haruko, you did great!

00:04:39.670 --> 00:04:41.340
Congratulations, Haruko!

00:04:41.340 --> 00:04:42.460
Thanks a lot!

00:04:42.460 --> 00:04:44.130
What would you like for dinner?

00:04:44.130 --> 00:04:46.510
You can have whatever you want to celebrate!

00:04:46.510 --> 00:04:48.920
I said we already ate!

00:04:48.920 --> 00:04:50.380
Right?

00:04:50.380 --> 00:04:53.550
Yeah... I'm going to take a shower.

00:05:07.210 --> 00:05:11.130
Haru! I'd like to take one, too, y'know!

00:05:11.130 --> 00:05:12.590
I'm coming out now!

00:05:29.550 --> 00:05:32.880
Oh, god, I looked down.

00:05:42.760 --> 00:05:44.670
I knew you'd be here.

00:05:44.670 --> 00:05:48.170
What're you doing, barging into my house uninvited?

00:05:48.170 --> 00:05:50.960
Well, I was going to borrow your shower.

00:05:50.960 --> 00:05:53.510
But Haruko's already using it.

00:05:57.510 --> 00:05:58.630
Here ya go.

00:06:02.760 --> 00:06:05.800
You need to take your medicine
to stop the inflammation.

00:06:05.800 --> 00:06:07.460
That's what your mom told me.

00:06:13.760 --> 00:06:19.170
Say, Haru, you tend to come here
when something's on your mind.

00:06:19.170 --> 00:06:21.300
So what's on yours, Kazu?

00:06:21.300 --> 00:06:22.590
Huh?

00:06:22.590 --> 00:06:25.800
Don't you come here when
something's bugging you?

00:06:27.630 --> 00:06:28.880
I guess!

00:06:30.880 --> 00:06:37.420
I feel like we've been lying around
up here ever since we were kids.

00:06:37.420 --> 00:06:38.210
Kazu.

00:06:38.210 --> 00:06:39.460
What?

00:06:39.460 --> 00:06:41.170
Was your grandma feeling well?

00:06:41.170 --> 00:06:42.800
She was doing great!

00:06:42.800 --> 00:06:47.050
No matter how many apples I peeled,
she ate so many that I couldn't keep up.

00:06:47.050 --> 00:06:48.920
Did she?

00:06:48.920 --> 00:06:50.840
Maybe I'll go with you next time.

00:06:50.840 --> 00:06:52.340
I said it's fine!

00:06:52.340 --> 00:06:54.920
I just talk my head off and then go home.

00:06:54.920 --> 00:06:57.460
Besides, isn't it amazing that Haruko
won the women's championship?

00:06:57.460 --> 00:06:59.380
She must be wicked strong.

00:07:04.630 --> 00:07:05.710
I wonder...

00:07:05.710 --> 00:07:07.260
Huh?

00:07:07.260 --> 00:07:09.960
Why'd I have to be born into
a family of judo specialists?

00:07:11.420 --> 00:07:13.960
So you're in sentimental mode.

00:07:13.960 --> 00:07:17.590
I knew I'd be relegated to the
sidelines with my shoulder like this.

00:07:17.590 --> 00:07:21.420
I'll never be as cool as my sister.

00:07:24.510 --> 00:07:25.760
Ow!

00:07:30.300 --> 00:07:32.170
You already are.

00:07:34.260 --> 00:07:37.550
Whenever you threw an opponent...

00:07:37.550 --> 00:07:40.380
...you looked like you'd been thrown yourself.

00:07:46.760 --> 00:07:50.800
That's what made your style of judo so cool.

00:08:01.300 --> 00:08:02.380
Rain?

00:08:02.380 --> 00:08:06.960
Whoa, a single drop of rain
fell on the tip of your nose.

00:08:06.960 --> 00:08:08.340
Uh, what?

00:08:08.340 --> 00:08:10.800
It's just like that urban legend.

00:08:10.800 --> 00:08:14.170
If a drop of rain hits you smack on the nose...

00:08:14.170 --> 00:08:17.010
...your wish will come true?

00:08:17.010 --> 00:08:20.050
Tomorrow you'll luck out
and take a perfect dump.

00:08:20.050 --> 00:08:22.090
What the hell are you talking about?

00:08:33.860 --> 00:08:35.870
School of
Sports Science
Offices

00:08:42.670 --> 00:08:45.880
Oh, Haru!

00:08:43.880 --> 00:08:45.540
School of
Sports Science
Offices

00:08:45.880 --> 00:08:47.210
See ya!

00:08:47.210 --> 00:08:50.710
What are you even doing here?

00:08:47.530 --> 00:08:49.170
School of
Sports Science
Offices

00:08:50.710 --> 00:08:53.090
Same thing as you.

00:08:55.880 --> 00:08:57.630
Is that you, Bandou?

00:08:57.630 --> 00:08:59.840
Uh, yes!

00:08:59.840 --> 00:09:00.960
Excuse me.

00:09:00.960 --> 00:09:02.260
Come in.

00:09:03.460 --> 00:09:08.340
I ran into Kaz... Hashimoto just now.

00:09:08.340 --> 00:09:11.300
What did he want?

00:09:11.300 --> 00:09:15.210
Seems he's going to quit the Judo Club.

00:09:15.210 --> 00:09:18.380
He assured me you'd come by
later to do the same thing,

00:09:18.380 --> 00:09:23.090
so I should listen to you.

00:09:23.090 --> 00:09:24.800
That's all he said.

00:09:36.300 --> 00:09:37.630
Kazu!

00:09:37.630 --> 00:09:39.010
Kazu!

00:09:41.260 --> 00:09:43.010
What's with you?

00:09:43.010 --> 00:09:45.670
What're you sprinting across campus for?

00:09:45.670 --> 00:09:47.670
You'll embarrass yourself.

00:09:47.670 --> 00:09:50.210
Why...

00:09:50.210 --> 00:09:51.920
Why are you doing this?

00:09:51.920 --> 00:09:54.510
Haru, you need to breathe.

00:09:54.510 --> 00:09:56.920
Why are you leaving, too?

00:09:56.920 --> 00:10:00.260
You don't need to quit judo!

00:10:04.010 --> 00:10:07.510
Anyway, just keep doing judo.

00:10:07.510 --> 00:10:09.510
You're plenty strong.

00:10:09.510 --> 00:10:12.710
During our sophomore year, you competed
in the inter-high school tournament.

00:10:12.710 --> 00:10:14.510
I lost in the second round.

00:10:14.510 --> 00:10:17.340
I didn't even participate!

00:10:18.590 --> 00:10:21.010
I've always worried about whether...

00:10:21.010 --> 00:10:24.840
...I'm good enough for Meishiin's Judo Club.

00:10:24.840 --> 00:10:30.590
Whether I was recruited just because
I'm a son of the Bandou Dojo.

00:10:30.590 --> 00:10:35.050
So I was so relieved when I hurt my shoulder.

00:10:35.050 --> 00:10:38.380
Because now I could quit judo.

00:10:38.380 --> 00:10:40.340
But you don't have any reason to--

00:10:40.340 --> 00:10:43.050
What are you talking about?

00:10:43.050 --> 00:10:45.840
When my parents died,

00:10:45.840 --> 00:10:48.260
and I transferred to your school...

00:10:49.920 --> 00:10:51.670
<b>ＫＡＺＵＭＡ ＨＡＳＨＩＭＯＴＯ</b>

00:10:51.670 --> 00:10:56.170
My Notebook
Keep Out!

00:10:52.510 --> 00:10:54.670
The very first friend I made...

00:11:01.840 --> 00:11:04.050
...was you.

00:11:04.050 --> 00:11:07.800
I started doing judo because you asked me to.

00:11:07.800 --> 00:11:08.430
Mutual Benefit

00:11:07.800 --> 00:11:08.340
I started doing judo because you asked me to.

00:11:08.340 --> 00:11:11.590
Haven't we always been together?

00:11:15.170 --> 00:11:16.380
So...

00:11:17.670 --> 00:11:20.130
That means we should quit together, too.

00:11:20.130 --> 00:11:21.460
What are you saying?

00:11:21.460 --> 00:11:22.170
Kazu, you're--

00:11:22.170 --> 00:11:25.340
Well, I made sure I timed it right.

00:11:25.340 --> 00:11:27.420
When exactly I would quit.

00:11:27.420 --> 00:11:28.670
Besides...

00:11:30.090 --> 00:11:34.090
I'm starting something new with you.

00:11:35.880 --> 00:11:37.880
Something new?

00:11:41.460 --> 00:11:43.630
Recruiting
new
members!!!

00:11:41.460 --> 00:11:43.630
Men's
Cheerleading

00:11:44.260 --> 00:11:46.710
Men's... cheerleading?!

00:11:58.090 --> 00:12:00.460
Please have a look!

00:12:00.460 --> 00:12:04.130
Come join the Men's Cheerleading Club!

00:12:04.130 --> 00:12:06.510
Haru, you need to be louder.

00:12:09.210 --> 00:12:10.880
Please...

00:12:12.130 --> 00:12:14.300
No, I can't do this!

00:12:14.300 --> 00:12:17.130
We won't recruit anyone with that attitude.

00:12:17.130 --> 00:12:22.340
Without more members,
we can't even start practicing.

00:12:22.340 --> 00:12:23.920
What do you mean "we"?

00:12:23.920 --> 00:12:26.340
I'm just helping you out.

00:12:26.340 --> 00:12:29.630
And besides, cheerleading's for girls!

00:12:29.630 --> 00:12:32.880
Nope, that's not true these days.

00:12:32.880 --> 00:12:35.130
Oh...?

00:12:35.130 --> 00:12:38.760
Whatever, I'm still not doing it!

00:12:38.760 --> 00:12:40.050
Oh!

00:12:40.050 --> 00:12:41.880
Hello there!

00:12:41.880 --> 00:12:46.590
We're recruiting members for
the Men's Cheerleading Club!

00:12:46.590 --> 00:12:50.960
Hello, we're the Men's Cheerleading Club!

00:12:50.960 --> 00:12:53.210
Hi there, we're the Men's Cheerleading Club!

00:12:55.840 --> 00:12:57.340
We're looking for new members!

00:12:57.340 --> 00:12:59.050
Definitely consider it!

00:13:00.630 --> 00:13:01.920
Well...

00:13:01.920 --> 00:13:03.170
I'll do it.

00:13:03.170 --> 00:13:06.130
Okay, next up is Building No. 10!

00:13:20.420 --> 00:13:21.760
I'm starving...

00:13:21.760 --> 00:13:26.170
Haru, I think I'll hand out fliers
in the cafeteria after this.

00:13:26.170 --> 00:13:27.670
Huh?

00:13:27.670 --> 00:13:31.800
We've been handing them out
all week without any luck.

00:13:31.800 --> 00:13:33.590
Nobody's interested.

00:13:33.590 --> 00:13:36.960
At this rate, it'll just be
the two of us forever.

00:13:36.960 --> 00:13:40.170
I already told you, I'm not doing it.

00:13:43.920 --> 00:13:47.630
Shouldn't we think of a better strategy?

00:13:47.630 --> 00:13:50.920
Then let's brainstorm at my place!

00:14:01.760 --> 00:14:03.920
Hey, watch where you're going.

00:14:03.920 --> 00:14:05.170
My apologies.

00:14:07.260 --> 00:14:08.710
Yeesh.

00:14:12.050 --> 00:14:14.260
Wanna hear something dumb?

00:14:14.260 --> 00:14:15.710
Sure.

00:14:15.710 --> 00:14:22.010
They say at 3AM during a full moon, the university's
statue comes to life. Think it's true?

00:14:22.010 --> 00:14:23.960
I doubt it.

00:14:23.960 --> 00:14:25.760
Hey, Haru, wanna grab some ice cream?

00:14:25.760 --> 00:14:27.010
Okay!

00:14:36.260 --> 00:14:40.050
I haven't been to your place in ages.

00:14:40.050 --> 00:14:42.880
It's still as shabby as ever.

00:14:42.880 --> 00:14:44.300
Oh, shut up.

00:14:44.300 --> 00:14:45.090
Let's go in.

00:14:45.090 --> 00:14:46.090
Let's.

00:14:53.420 --> 00:14:55.880
Who's that? A friend of yours?

00:14:55.880 --> 00:14:57.630
Nope.

00:14:57.630 --> 00:14:59.710
I am Wataru Mizoguchi.

00:14:59.710 --> 00:15:01.710
I am no one's friend.

00:15:08.630 --> 00:15:09.960
It's sweltering.

00:15:09.960 --> 00:15:12.090
We'll have to open a window.

00:15:12.090 --> 00:15:13.630
Allow me.

00:15:27.170 --> 00:15:28.840
It won't open.

00:15:28.840 --> 00:15:31.340
More importantly, who are you?

00:15:31.340 --> 00:15:34.130
I believe I just said my name
was Wataru Mizoguchi.

00:15:34.130 --> 00:15:37.380
No, that's not what I meant...

00:15:37.380 --> 00:15:41.550
I've never seen you play the straight
man to someone you've just met.

00:15:41.550 --> 00:15:45.260
That's because he's so difficult
to communicate with.

00:15:45.260 --> 00:15:46.760
Thank you.

00:15:46.760 --> 00:15:48.300
That wasn't a compliment.

00:15:55.840 --> 00:15:59.960
Wataru Mizoguchi. First-year business
school student. 20 years old.

00:15:59.960 --> 00:16:04.010
I received this flier the other day.

00:16:04.010 --> 00:16:06.760
It intrigued me, so I tried to talk to you,

00:16:06.760 --> 00:16:09.130
but I kept missing my chance to do so all week,

00:16:09.130 --> 00:16:10.800
and then I came here.

00:16:10.800 --> 00:16:12.760
That's a lot of missed chances.

00:16:12.760 --> 00:16:16.590
"Do not suppose opportunity
will knock twice at your door."

00:16:16.590 --> 00:16:20.210
Dixit French moralist Nicolas Chamfort.

00:16:20.210 --> 00:16:23.010
I knew it the moment I laid eyes on this flier.

00:16:23.010 --> 00:16:25.380
"My opportunity has come knocking."

00:16:25.380 --> 00:16:29.670
So I decided to open the door.

00:16:29.670 --> 00:16:33.210
I enjoy trying new things.

00:16:33.210 --> 00:16:37.960
I want to challenge myself to do
something no one else has done!

00:16:37.960 --> 00:16:41.420
"Become a hero by supporting someone else."

00:16:41.420 --> 00:16:44.800
"Gain the strength to inspire someone..."

00:16:44.800 --> 00:16:46.510
"...to greater heights."

00:16:47.670 --> 00:16:48.960
Uh...

00:16:48.960 --> 00:16:53.050
Hey, what made you want to do
men's cheerleading in the first place?

00:16:53.050 --> 00:16:55.050
I, too, would like to know.

00:17:03.920 --> 00:17:06.840
This is the first time you've seen this, Haru.

00:17:06.840 --> 00:17:09.210
And I as well.

00:17:09.210 --> 00:17:12.630
That's because we literally just met.

00:17:14.630 --> 00:17:17.090
That's...

00:17:17.090 --> 00:17:19.170
Yup.

00:17:19.170 --> 00:17:20.670
My parents.

00:17:23.260 --> 00:17:25.920
What a lovely photo.

00:17:25.920 --> 00:17:29.630
My mom was a cheerleader.

00:17:29.630 --> 00:17:35.210
She joined the Cheerleading Club
in college, and my dad was the coach.

00:17:35.210 --> 00:17:39.050
So they got married while
she was still a student.

00:17:39.050 --> 00:17:42.630
Mom started cheerleading
when she was in high school,

00:17:42.630 --> 00:17:45.460
and she was crazy about it after that.

00:17:45.460 --> 00:17:51.090
Her team even competed in world championships
back when they had sponsors.

00:17:51.090 --> 00:17:55.260
She told me about it a million times
while I was growing up:

00:17:55.260 --> 00:18:02.260
"A cheerleader supports everyone,
inspires them, makes them smile."

00:18:03.420 --> 00:18:07.670
I want to fly high like she did.

00:18:07.670 --> 00:18:11.670
I want to move people like she did.

00:18:13.590 --> 00:18:16.210
Understood. Let's do it.

00:18:16.210 --> 00:18:19.210
We will cheer. And we will fly!

00:18:20.260 --> 00:18:22.800
Are you free tomorrow?

00:18:45.130 --> 00:18:46.880
Let's go, Sparks!

00:18:59.010 --> 00:19:03.050
Isn't it so much more impressive in person?

00:19:03.050 --> 00:19:04.210
Uh, it's...

00:19:04.210 --> 00:19:06.210
It is!

00:19:06.210 --> 00:19:10.090
People tend to think
cheerleading's only for girls.

00:19:10.090 --> 00:19:12.420
So did I!

00:19:13.460 --> 00:19:17.710
There are mixed teams, like Sparks here,

00:19:17.710 --> 00:19:21.920
but I want to try it with an all-men's one.

00:19:23.170 --> 00:19:27.920
I'm sure it will be a
dynamic, fresh, fun team...

00:19:27.920 --> 00:19:30.380
...the likes of which no one has ever seen!

00:19:43.710 --> 00:19:45.760
Go, Sparks!

00:19:57.050 --> 00:19:59.130
Well? Let's do it.

00:19:59.130 --> 00:20:00.670
Uh, I...

00:20:00.670 --> 00:20:01.840
No way, no way!

00:20:01.840 --> 00:20:03.050
I mean, I'm afraid of--

00:20:03.050 --> 00:20:04.130
I'm not afraid.

00:20:04.130 --> 00:20:05.130
So long as we do it together.

00:20:05.130 --> 00:20:06.210
Huh?

00:20:06.210 --> 00:20:08.210
No, I can't do that!

00:20:08.210 --> 00:20:12.010
It'll be fine, we can handle it.

00:20:12.010 --> 00:20:14.800
Don't be so sure.

00:20:14.800 --> 00:20:19.670
Do you have any idea how long
it takes to get that good?

00:20:19.670 --> 00:20:21.920
And an all-men's team?

00:20:21.920 --> 00:20:23.050
Don't be ridiculous.

00:20:23.050 --> 00:20:26.550
You plan on calling yourselves
The Three Stooges?

00:20:26.550 --> 00:20:30.630
If you're just doing this
for funsies, then give up now.

00:20:33.510 --> 00:20:36.920
We won't know if we can do it unless we try.

00:20:36.920 --> 00:20:38.010
Oh!

00:20:38.010 --> 00:20:40.550
So you're gonna join the
Cheerleading Club, Haru!

00:20:40.550 --> 00:20:42.050
Let's do it!

00:20:42.050 --> 00:20:43.840
No, I...

00:20:43.840 --> 00:20:46.960
I think you're meant for cheerleading.

00:20:46.960 --> 00:20:50.380
Your cheering is powerful in a way.

00:20:51.710 --> 00:20:55.210
Your cheering has a kind of power behind it.

00:21:00.920 --> 00:21:04.420
I guess I could give it a shot.

00:21:04.420 --> 00:21:06.840
I knew you'd say that!

00:21:06.840 --> 00:21:08.710
Then we have our third member.

00:21:08.710 --> 00:21:09.510
What?

00:21:09.510 --> 00:21:11.420
Why am I the third one?!

00:21:11.420 --> 00:21:13.630
That should be you!

00:21:13.630 --> 00:21:16.670
I decided to join the moment I saw the flier,

00:21:16.670 --> 00:21:18.960
so I beat you to it.

00:21:21.550 --> 00:21:23.210
Thanks a lot.

00:21:24.380 --> 00:21:26.710
Now the three of us can...

00:21:34.630 --> 00:21:35.920
Start!

00:21:35.920 --> 00:21:44.010
"In the life of a young man, the most essential
thing for happiness is the gift of friendship."

00:21:44.010 --> 00:21:47.090
Dixit Sir William Osler.

00:21:47.090 --> 00:21:48.340
Who?

00:21:50.960 --> 00:21:53.550
Let's go through the motions!

00:21:53.550 --> 00:21:54.760
First a Low V!

00:21:54.760 --> 00:21:55.840
High V!

00:21:55.840 --> 00:21:57.460
Punch!

00:21:57.460 --> 00:21:59.760
These are all basic cheerleading positions.

00:21:59.760 --> 00:22:01.340
Now, Toe-Touch!

00:22:01.340 --> 00:22:02.260
Toe-Touch!

00:22:02.260 --> 00:22:03.590
Toe-Touch!

00:22:03.590 --> 00:22:07.880
I studied these in a book once,
but I can't actually do any of them.

00:22:07.880 --> 00:22:10.590
I can't... This is too embarr--

00:22:10.590 --> 00:22:12.880
Right, let's give it a go!

00:22:12.880 --> 00:22:15.300
Now, all together!

00:22:15.300 --> 00:22:16.550
Low V!

00:22:16.550 --> 00:22:17.550
High V!

00:22:17.550 --> 00:22:19.670
Punch!

00:22:19.670 --> 00:22:21.170
What are they doing?

00:22:21.170 --> 00:22:22.760
A dance?

00:22:22.760 --> 00:22:24.420
Nope!

00:22:24.420 --> 00:22:25.880
We're...

00:22:25.880 --> 00:22:28.300
...the Men's Cheerleading Club!

00:22:28.990 --> 00:22:32.960
The Curtain Rises

00:22:49.760 --> 00:22:55.420
<i>I'll put an end to spending</i>
<i>my days so thoughtlessly</i>

00:22:55.420 --> 00:22:59.460
<i>I'm dying to break free of this</i>

00:22:59.460 --> 00:23:05.170
<i>Since I can never take that first step forward,</i>

00:23:05.170 --> 00:23:09.260
<i>you always take my hand and pull me along</i>

00:23:09.260 --> 00:23:15.090
<i>You've brought me to see</i>
<i>something completely new</i>

00:23:15.090 --> 00:23:17.380
<i>My whole world is changing</i>

00:23:17.380 --> 00:23:20.630
<i>With that first step</i>

00:23:20.630 --> 00:23:23.800
<i>I felt transformed</i>

00:23:23.800 --> 00:23:28.760
<i>I can go anywhere; it'll work</i>
<i>out so long as we're together</i>

00:23:28.760 --> 00:23:30.340
<i>Go on, fly high, </i>

00:23:30.340 --> 00:23:31.960
<i>just as you are</i>

00:23:31.960 --> 00:23:35.130
<i>At times you'll feel lost and scared,</i>

00:23:35.130 --> 00:23:41.630
<i>but there are so many things you</i>
<i>won't know if you never give them a go</i>

00:23:41.630 --> 00:23:43.260
<i>Go on, fly high, </i>

00:23:43.260 --> 00:23:48.130
<i>stretch out your hands until</i>
<i>you're almost touching the sky</i>

00:23:48.130 --> 00:23:51.380
<i>We're not alone anymore</i>

00:23:51.380 --> 00:23:56.510
<i>Together we'll fly into a new world</i>

00:24:03.670 --> 00:24:06.960
You there, want to try something new?

00:24:06.960 --> 00:24:09.510
How about you, want to do something cool?

00:24:09.510 --> 00:24:13.920
Why not try cheering your heart out with us?

00:24:13.920 --> 00:24:15.960
Haru, here we go.

00:24:15.960 --> 00:24:20.960
Next Episode: Your First Cheerleader Smile

00:24:15.960 --> 00:24:18.960
Next Episode: Your First Cheerleader Smile.

00:24:18.960 --> 00:24:20.960
Go! Fight! Win!
